---
import TextPage from "../layouts/TextPage.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from "../lib/site";
---

<TextPage
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`The privacy policy of ${SITE_NAME}: what information the site does and does not collect.`}
  intro="In short: this site does not ask for personal information and does not track you."
  updated="November 20, 2026"
>
  <h2>What we collect from visitors</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE_NAME} has no accounts, forms or comments, and it does not set cookies or use analytics or advertising trackers. We do
    not ask you for your name, email address or any other personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Technical logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is delivered through Amazon Web Services. Like any web host, the service may keep standard technical records of
    requests, for example the address of the device that asked for a page, the page, and the time, for security and to keep the
    site running. We do not use these records to identify individual visitors.
  </p>

  <h2>The listing data we show</h2>
  <p>
    The prices, titles and cities on this site come from public Facebook Marketplace listings. We do not show seller names or
    profiles, listing photos or descriptions, and we link to the original listing on Facebook.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Pages link to listings on Facebook. When you follow a link, the other site's own privacy practices apply, not this policy.
  </p>

  <h2>If this changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we later add analytics, cookies, advertising or email alerts, we will update this policy before they start and say what
    information is involved. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy or a request about your information: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
